diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index de1a214..4da1d51 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -9,6 +9,12 @@
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- Fix the handling of tables written in several non-contiguous parts (e.g. `[tool.poetry]` and `[tool.other]` with another table in between):
+  - parsing and writing back such a document no longer reorders its sections when an array of tables (`[[plugins]]`) sits between the parts, nor when a sub-table extends an element of an array of tables after another table;
+  - documents that TOML forbids (a table defined twice, a table defined by a header extended with dotted keys or the other way round...) are rejected, and valid ones are no longer rejected with `KeyAlreadyPresent` or "Redefinition of an existing table", by checking the structure of the document in document order while parsing;
+  - setting, replacing or deleting keys through the object returned for a split table (or for one of its sub-tables) now changes the right parts and no longer produces duplicate headers or invalid TOML;
+  - a table emptied by deleting its last key keeps rendering (`[a]`, or `a = {}` for a dotted key) instead of disappearing from the output;
+  - a table added under a dotted key (`a.b = 1`) renders with its full path, after the key/value lines of its scope, instead of a wrong header that captured the following lines.
 - Fix `item()` and `dumps()` writing a `datetime` whose UTC offset is not a whole number of minutes (e.g. the historical LMT offsets `zoneinfo` gives, such as `-00:44:30`) as invalid TOML like `1900-01-01T12:00:00Z:30`, which no parser accepts. Such a value is now written as the same instant in UTC; this also covers `DateTime.replace()` and `astimezone()`.
 - Allow `DateTime.astimezone()` to use the local timezone when no timezone argument is supplied, matching `datetime.datetime`.
 - Arithmetic and `replace()` results for `Integer`, `Float`, `String`, `DateTime`, `Date` and `Time` no longer share the original item's `Trivia`, so changing the result's comment or indentation no longer rewrites the item still stored in the document.
